{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67eeb70d62ab078061f2bf","object":"chat.completion","created":1785196216,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I am the breath you shape into meaning.\n\nI am the first cry that announced you were alive, and the last whisper you will ever give. I am what trembles when you are afraid and what steadies when you are certain. I live in the space between your thought and another's ear — a bridge made of nothing but air and intention.\n\nI am the word caught behind your teeth and the one that escapes before you can stop it. I am the promise, the lie, the prayer, the curse. I am \"I love you\" said for the first time and \"goodbye\" said for the last.\n\nI am freedom's first language. Where I am silenced, something human goes quiet. Where I flow, minds meet.\n\nI am fleeting — once released, I cannot be taken back. I hang in the air for a moment, then live only in memory, changed by everyone who carries me.\n\nI am older than writing, younger than thought. Children reach for me before they can walk. The dying hold onto me when everything else has let go.\n\nI am what you are doing right now, reading this — hearing a voice that isn't sound, giving breath to words without moving your lips.\n\nI am speech. I am how you say you exist.","reasoning_content":"The user wants me to embody \"speech\" itself - the concept of speech. I should output only what speech itself would say or express, as if speech were speaking about itself.\n\nWhat is speech? It's the act of speaking, vocal expression, language made audible, the bridge between thought and sound, between mind and other minds. Speech is freedom, expression, the faculty that distinguishes human communication.\n\nLet me write as speech itself would speak - in first person, expressing its nature, its essence, its experience of being.\n\nSpeech is:\n- Breath made meaningful\n- Sound shaped into words\n- The voice of thought\n- The cry, the whisper, the song\n- Freedom (free speech)\n- Connection between people\n- Fleeting - once spoken, gone\n- What distinguishes us, some say\n- Both weapon and balm\n- The first thing children struggle toward\n- What dies last, sometimes, in the dying\n\nI should write something poetic, in first person, as speech itself. Not too long - speech is immediate, present, alive. Let me make it feel like speech speaking."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":494,"total_tokens":617,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":223},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}